{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/816600-spirit-that-claim","id":816600,"title":"Spirit that Claim","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-25T19:41:36-08:00","id":816600,"title":"Spirit that Claim","content":"Someone spoke to me about a new version of Claim. Spirit can Urge, materialize, do possession, but my friend insisted that he saw somewhere, something about a stronger version of claiming that was like irreversible, even with abjuration or gift like banish. Since he was very insistent, I checked everywhere, but did not find anything on the subject. Anyone knows if something similar to what I am describing exist or has indeed, existed in the past ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T19:48:28-08:00","id":816605,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the Forge Herald ability?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T20:06:18-08:00","id":816613,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that this is a natural result of long term possession. There are cases discussed in the antagonist section of the Forsaken (1ed) book where the spirit and individual were so well suited to each other that they 'merged' into a new, singular being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T20:17:20-08:00","id":816620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/816600-spirit-that-claim?p=816613#post816613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that this is a natural result of long term possession. There are cases discussed in the antagonist section of the Forsaken (1ed) book where the spirit and individual were so well suited to each other that they 'merged' into a new, singular being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that just what Claiming is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T22:51:51-08:00","id":816686,"title":"","content":"Maybe it was a Strix possession? Either way, if the possession lasts long enough the mortal dies when separated, its body too ravaged by the spirit to survive on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T23:43:47-08:00","id":816705,"title":"","content":"I feel like there's some serious miscommunication going on here somewhere. So I'm going to take a step back and lay some groundwork so I know we're all working from the same base assumptions. I apologize if this comes off like I'm explaining something you already know, but it seems like we're talking right past each other so I just want to make sure we're using the same terminology,<br /> <br /> In order for an ephemeral entity such as a spirit to influence a living being, the being must be under the prerequisite Condition associated with the ephemeral entity's type (Resonant for spirits, Anchor for ghosts, Infrastructure for angels). The entity can then use the Strengthen Influence effect to place the Open Condition on the subject. An Open subject can be further manipulated in one of three ways: Urging, Possession, or Claiming.<br /> <br /> In order to Urge the subject, the entity needs to Fetter itself to them, using the Fetter Manifestation. This places the Fettered Condition on the entity and the Urged Condition on the subject. An Urged subject is not under the entity's direct control, but the entity can read the subject's mind and implant suggestions, which the subject is tempted to follow but not forced to.<br /> <br /> In order to Possess the subject, all the entity needs to do is use the Possess Manifestation. This places the Possessed Condition on the subject. A Possessed subject is under the entity's direct control, though the subject retains enough awareness to resist the entity's influence, inflicting penalties on the rolls the entity forces them to make. If the entity also Fetters itself to the subject, these penalties decrease over time. The longer the entity remains Fettered to the subject, the harder the subject finds it to resist.<br /> <br /> In order to Claim the subject, the entity needs to have Possessed the subject several times. Once the prerequisite number of Possessions is met, the entity can use the Control Influence effect to place the Controlled Condition on the subject. The Controlled Condition doesn't do anything on its own, but it is a prerequisite for the entity to Claim the subject, (just as Open is a prerequisite to Urge or Possess the subject.) Once the subject has the Controlled Condition, the entity can use the Claim Manifestation to place the Claimed Condition on the subject. A Claimed subject merges with the entity completely. There is no need for the entity to control the subject's actions, because there is no subject and no entity any more; they exist as a single amalgamation of flesh and spirit, with a single consciousness and a shared will. This state is permanent, unless the amalgamate itself decides to separate back into two beings, tearing its own ephemera from its matter and becoming an ephemeral entity and living creature once again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T02:20:19-08:00","id":816754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/816600-spirit-that-claim?p=816705#post816705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once the prerequisite number of Possessions is met, the entity can use the Control Influence effect to place the Controlled Condition on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that the multiple possessions/ control influence was a case of &quot;<i>or&quot;, </i>not &quot;and&quot;. Primarily because requiring the control influence be used cuts off claiming to anything less than rank 3, which is blatantly not the case in the examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T06:28:08-08:00","id":816827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once the prerequisite number of Possessions is met, the entity can use the Control Influence effect to place the Controlled Condition on the subject. </div> </div> </div>From what I can see, the controlled condition only requires the prerequisite number of possessions. In addition, it seems that Control Influence shifting the Open Condition to Controlled does not require the prerequisite number of possessions, and is simply a quick fix method of doing it rather than doing it the proper way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T09:43:10-08:00","id":816950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/816600-spirit-that-claim?p=816754#post816754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that the multiple possessions/ control influence was a case of &quot;<i>or&quot;, </i>not &quot;and&quot;. Primarily because requiring the control influence be used cuts off claiming to anything less than rank 3, which is blatantly not the case in the examples.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/816600-spirit-that-claim?p=816827#post816827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I can see, the controlled condition only requires the prerequisite number of possessions. In addition, it seems that Control Influence shifting the Open Condition to Controlled does not require the prerequisite number of possessions, and is simply a quick fix method of doing it rather than doing it the proper way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The flowchart makes it seem that way, but the &quot;Causing the Condition&quot; section of the Controlled Condition seems to indicate otherwise. Regardless, the point is that Claiming is the entity permanently fusing itself with the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-26-2016, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T13:43:48-08:00","id":817119,"title":"","content":"So, do Ghost Claimings function like Spirit ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T13:46:58-08:00","id":817124,"title":"","content":"Usually. Occasionally you get Sin-Eaters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T14:18:47-08:00","id":817162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/816600-spirit-that-claim?p=816950#post816950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The flowchart makes it seem that way, but the &quot;Causing the Condition&quot; section of the Controlled Condition seems to indicate otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the &quot;Causing the Condition&quot; section of the Controlled Condition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Condition is the result<br /> of repeated use of the Possess Manifestation Effect by the<br /> causing spirit. It must have succeeded in possessing the<br /> subject on a number of separate occasions equal to the<br /> Willpower of spirit or subject (whichever is higher).</div> </div> </div> </div>I see nothing about influences here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T14:20:07-08:00","id":817165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/816600-spirit-that-claim?p=816950#post816950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The flowchart makes it seem that way, but the &quot;Causing the Condition&quot; section of the Controlled Condition seems to indicate otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>No... the causing the condition section doesn't even mention using influence to get the controlled condition. It says it's caused by using possession over and over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T14:26:22-08:00","id":817170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/816600-spirit-that-claim?p=817162#post817162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see nothing about influences here.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/816600-spirit-that-claim?p=817165#post817165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No... the causing the condition section doesn't even mention using influence to get the controlled condition. It says it's caused by using possession over and over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. The Condition doesn't say that it can be caused by the Control Influence. Therefore, I assume repeated possession is always required to cause the Condition, since it doesn't list any other means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T14:29:02-08:00","id":817175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/816600-spirit-that-claim?p=817124#post817124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usually. Occasionally you get Sin-Eaters.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, Dave has mentioned that the Bargain is probably its own Manifestation effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T14:30:56-08:00","id":817176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/816600-spirit-that-claim?p=817175#post817175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIRC, Dave has mentioned that the Bargain is probably its own Manifestation effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat! <span style=\"color:white\">six more characters</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T17:01:27-08:00","id":817252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/816600-spirit-that-claim?p=817170#post817170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. The Condition doesn't say that it can be caused by the Control Influence. Therefore, I assume repeated possession is always required to cause the Condition, since it doesn't list any other means.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it just doesn't work. The Devourer Hound on page 209 has an essence pool of 10 and one dot of influence, which means it is <i>definitely </i>claimed by a rank 1 spirit. Under the system you're proposing, no spirit under rank 3 could claim something under <i>any circumstance. </i>Ergo, NO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T17:14:19-08:00","id":817258,"title":"","content":"Describing the Control Influence power, 'The spirit can make dramatic changes within its sphere of influence; twist emotions entirely; or dictate an animal\u2019s actions, a plant\u2019s growth, or an object\u2019s functioning. This Influence can shift the Open Condition to Controlled for its duration. The cost is 3 Essence.'<br /> <br /> As for the Devourer Hound, the write-up suggests it's not exactly a voluntary claiming, 'The Processing Plant\u2019s owners then bind these spirits and force them to Claim the hounds, creating a steady flow of expendable monstrosities. The story\u2019s hard to believe, but it might explain the growing numbers of Devourer Hounds in the region.'<br /> <br /> While a rank 1 spirit may not be able to use Control normally, if the area is under the effect of the Wellspring rite and the spirit is considered a pack member it can act as if it had a higher Influence. Presumably there are other methods that could be used as well, and an idigam can just shove them in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T17:24:23-08:00","id":817261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/816600-spirit-that-claim?p=817258#post817258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While a rank 1 spirit may not be able to use Control normally, if the area is under the effect of the Wellspring rite and the spirit is considered a pack member it can act as if it had a higher Influence. Presumably there are other methods that could be used as well, and an idigam can just shove them in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe nofather is correct. The binding ritual used seems to be the cause of the early claiming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T17:51:13-08:00","id":817281,"title":"","content":"Frankly, the precise means required to achieve the Controlled Condition are completely tangential to my point, which was simply that this &quot;new type of Claiming&quot; that permanently merges the spirit with its host and gives it more complete control than Possession is not new at all. That's just how Claiming works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}